GitHub Copilot CLI screens in this folder are plain-text (no colour) for harnesses/copilot.toml.

Every *-src.txt file here is CONSTRUCTED, not a capture. Each is built from short UI strings in
GitHub Copilot CLI 1.0.109 for darwin/arm64 (npm `@github/copilot` 1.0.109, tarball sha256
9565e94019b8c24ca4b4f6fc7dd3231b3d4ae509ec660b7e643d0b93a5d3b230, and
`@github/copilot-darwin-arm64` 1.0.109, tarball sha256
d00563d5481e8a275b41f78eeb71e19a90309a908255575293bf55e9778cc37a; its embedded cli-main.js,
sha256 44a03c6501820d7a1e8bc8ad46fa060f8d9a9257ec81cbb0f1f15b289bc801d1), read as text only,
never run. Licence: the GitHub Copilot CLI License (proprietary, GitHub). Only short UI strings
are transcribed; no code is copied.

idle-src.txt: a reply line, the prompt row (rail `┃`, glyph `❯ `, nothing typed), the hint row
`/ commands · ? help` drawn only under an empty prompt, and a status line.
idle-typed-src.txt: idle-src.txt with text typed in the prompt row and no hint row.
working-src.txt: idle-src.txt with the busy row `◐ Thinking  ctrl+c interrupt` above the prompt.
unknown-exitwarn-src.txt: idle-src.txt with the hint row replaced by the exit warning after one
Ctrl+C at an empty prompt (`ctrl+c again to exit`).
waiting_for_approval-shell-src.txt, waiting_for_approval-edit-src.txt: a command and a file edit
approval in a round-border box (`╭─╮`, `│`, `╰─╯`), first row `❯ 1. Yes` selected, the reject row
`No, and tell Copilot what to do differently (Esc to stop)` last. The box is 60 columns; rows
longer than that run past its right edge here.
waiting_for_approval-url-src.txt: a URL access approval (`Do you want to allow this access?`,
reject row `Something else, and tell Copilot what to do differently (Esc to stop)`).
waiting_for_approval-plan-src.txt: the plan approval (title `Plan Ready for Review`, `Accept plan
and continue in ... execution mode` rows, last row `Suggest changes`).
unknown-trust-src.txt: the folder-trust menu (`Confirm folder trust`) in a round-border box.
unknown-login-src.txt: the sign-in account picker (`What account do you want to log into?`).

None of these is a real screen. A real screen added here by a live run is named *-real.txt.

U-R1B-COPILOT-LAYOUT: Copilot 1.0.109 draws its composer in one of two forms. Form A (prompt frame
on) is a rail: a `╻` row of `▄`, one `┃ ` row per input line (no `❯` glyph), a `╹` row of `▀`.
Form B (prompt frame off) is a rule of `─`, the row `❯ ` (or `! ` in shell mode) with the input, and
a rule of `─`. In both the status row sits above the composer and one hint row under it. The frame
is on when COPILOT_PROMPT_FRAME=1, off when it is 0, and otherwise follows the PROMPT_FRAME feature
flag (not in Apple Terminal, and only when the theme's background colours are known); the flag's
default is served at run time and could not be read from the package. The files below are
constructed from cli-main.js 1.0.109 strings (same sha256 as above), not captures.
